Operational Feasibility Analysis

Operational feasibility analysis determines whether the proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform will be practical, easy to use, accepted by users, maintainable, and beneficial in real-world situations.

The proposed system is operationally feasible because it provides a simple and interactive platform that users can access through a web browser. The system is designed to improve cybersecurity awareness and help users identify and prevent phishing attacks.

Factor | Assessment | Remarks
User Acceptance | High | Cybersecurity awareness is useful and relevant for users
Ease of Use | High | Simple and interactive user interface
Training Requirement | Low | Minimal technical knowledge is required
Accessibility | High | The platform can be accessed through a web browser
Maintainability | High | Modular design simplifies maintenance
User Engagement | High | Simulations and quizzes improve learning
Educational Benefit | High | Improves cybersecurity awareness


User Acceptance

The proposed system is expected to have high user acceptance because cybersecurity awareness is important for people who use digital platforms and the internet.

Users can benefit from learning how to identify phishing attacks, suspicious emails, malicious links, fake websites, and other fraudulent activities.

The interactive nature of the platform can encourage users to actively participate in cybersecurity awareness training.


Ease of Use

The system will provide a simple and user-friendly interface.

Users will be able to:

- Access cybersecurity awareness training material.
- Learn about phishing attacks.
- Participate in phishing simulations.
- Attempt interactive quizzes.
- View their performance.
- Receive feedback based on their results.

The system will be designed so that users can easily understand and navigate its features.


Training Requirement

Users do not require advanced technical knowledge to operate the proposed system.

The platform will provide clear instructions and a simple interface for accessing different features.

Therefore, the training requirement for users is minimal.


Accessibility

The proposed system can be accessed through a web browser.

Users with a computer or other supported device and an internet connection can access the platform.

The web-based nature of the system improves accessibility and convenience.


Maintainability

The proposed system can be developed using a modular structure.

Different components of the system can be maintained independently.

The major modules may include:

- User Authentication Module.
- Training Module.
- Phishing Simulation Module.
- Quiz Module.
- Performance Assessment Module.

This modular design simplifies maintenance and makes future updates easier.


User Engagement

Interactive features such as phishing simulations and quizzes can improve user engagement.

Instead of only reading theoretical information, users can actively participate in learning activities and test their knowledge.

This practical approach can help users better understand phishing attacks and improve their ability to identify suspicious activities.


Operational Benefits

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform provides several benefits:

- Improves cybersecurity awareness.
- Helps users identify phishing attacks.
- Provides practical learning experiences.
- Encourages safe internet practices.
- Allows users to evaluate their knowledge.
- Provides feedback for improvement.

Therefore, the proposed system is operationally feasible and beneficial for users.



Analysis

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform addresses the growing problem of phishing attacks and the lack of cybersecurity awareness among users.

The system provides an educational and practical environment where users can learn about phishing attacks and practice identifying suspicious activities. Interactive simulations and quizzes can improve user engagement compared to traditional theoretical awareness methods.

The technical and operational feasibility analysis indicates that the project can be successfully implemented using available technologies and resources.


Observation

Clearly defining the problem, objectives, scope, and feasibility requirements provides a strong foundation for software design and development.

The proposed Cybersecurity Awareness Platform is focused on solving a real-world problem by improving users' ability to recognize and prevent phishing attacks.



Result

The problem statement, project objectives, project scope, and feasibility requirements for the Cybersecurity Awareness Platform were successfully identified and prepared.

The proposed solution is practical and provides an effective approach for improving cybersecurity awareness related to phishing detection and prevention.